  "answer": "I added a page to \"Stocks I watch\", but it can't fetch live prices from Yahoo Finance. Pages run in a sandbox with no network access, so any call to Yahoo would be blocked.\n\nInstead, the page has a \"Now\" price box next to each ticker. You type in the current price and it works out the profit in money and as a percentage for each stock. It also shows total cost, total value and total profit. It reads your AAPL, NVDA and VOLV-B rows from the note, so new rows appear automatically. The prices you enter are saved on that device. I didn't change the note's text.\n\nIf you'd rather have the prices in the note itself, I can add a \"Current price\" column and have the page read it from there.",
